      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}+3$ for $x>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= \\int x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= \\frac{x^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+3\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+3x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
